  "text-ergebnisse.tex": {
   "lines": [
    "Calciumoxalat-Monohydrat (synthetisch) loses mass in 3 steps: \\labval{tga-calciumoxalat-monohydrat-synthetisch}{step1-loss} (peak \\labval{tga-calciumoxalat-monohydrat-synthetisch}{step1-peak}), \\labval{tga-calciumoxalat-monohydrat-synthetisch}{step2-loss} (peak \\labval{tga-calciumoxalat-monohydrat-synthetisch}{step2-peak}), \\labval{tga-calciumoxalat-monohydrat-synthetisch}{step3-loss} (peak \\labval{tga-calciumoxalat-monohydrat-synthetisch}{step3-peak}). 5~\\% mass loss is reached at \\labval{tga-calciumoxalat-monohydrat-synthetisch}{t5}. The residue is \\labval{tga-calciumoxalat-monohydrat-synthetisch}{residue}. The calcium oxalate check passed."
   ],
   "type": "tex"
  },
  "text-methodik.tex": {
   "lines": [
    "Run Calciumoxalat-Monohydrat (synthetisch)~\\cite{data-tga-calciumoxalat-monohydrat-synthetisch} (sample mass 10.000~mg, heating rate 10.0~K/min, atmosphere N$_2$, crucible Al2O3) was evaluated according to ISO~11358-1~\\cite{tga-iso11358-1}. The DTG was calculated with a Savitzky-Golay filter~\\cite{tga-savgol} over about 4~K. Steps were taken from the peaks of the mass loss rate; the extrapolated onset and endset are the intersections of the tangent at the inflection point of the TG curve over temperature (local slope dm/dT) with the extended baseline before and after the step. Contents were calculated from theoretical decomposition losses (IUPAC atomic weights~\\cite{tga-ciaaw2021,tga-brown2001}).",
    "",
    "The following own equations were also evaluated:",
    "\\[ n = \\frac{\\frac{L_{1}}{100} \\cdot 146.11}{18.015} = 0.9851 \\] \\cite{eq-brown-2001-69f95}"
   ],
   "type": "tex"
  },
